{"id": "27", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "To fix a door that won't lock, first try to align the door latch with the hole in the strike plate. If the latch is misaligned, you can perform a lipstick test to see where the latch contacts the strike plate. If it contacts too high or too low, tighten all the door's hinge screws. You may also need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb or move the strike plate. If this doesn't work, shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, pry it up until it comes loose and remove it. Replace the door stop back on the jamb, set back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 97.821, "generation_time_seconds": 67.5039, "selection_time_seconds": 30.3149, "nemotron": {"method": "gd", "step_beam_size": 2, "num_rollout": 4, "num_foresight": 3, "runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code"}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "28", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "To fix a door that won't lock, you can try the following steps based on the given passages:\n1. Close the door and attempt to lock it.\n2. If it doesn't lock, open the door and use a chisel to tap and pry off the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Remove the top door stop as well.\n3. Place the door stop back on the jamb, aligning it 1/4 inch from its original location using the distinct line left behind.\n4. Nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on.\n5. If the latch still doesn't catch, tighten the hinges first.\n6. Enlarge the latch hole in the jamb if necessary.\n7. Enlarge the strike plate hole or move the strike plate if the latch doesn't align with it.\n8. Ensure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\nFollowing these steps should help fix the door lock issue.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 92.647, "generation_time_seconds": 61.844, "selection_time_seconds": 30.8006, "nemotron": {"method": "gd", "step_beam_size": 2, "num_rollout": 4, "num_foresight": 3, "runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code"}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.56, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "35", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "To cook pollock, first, preheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Then, season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Next, place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes, or until the fish flakes easily. If desired, you can also add cheese on top of the pollock fillets and bake for an additional 3 minutes to melt the cheese.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nI need to examine the given passages to determine if they contain any information about cooking pollock. If the passages do not include cooking instructions, ingredients, methods, or any relevant details about preparing pollock, then I must conclude that the information is insufficient to answer the question. I will carefully analyze the content of the passages to check for any mention of cooking pollock, including preparation steps, cooking times, temperatures, seasonings, or serving suggestions. If no such information is found, I will determine that the passages do not provide enough detail to formulate an answer.\nI will now carefully examine the provided passages for any information related to cooking pollock. I will specifically look for details such as cooking methods (e.g., baking, frying, steaming), required ingredients, preparation steps, cooking times, temperatures, or any other relevant culinary instructions. I will check whether the passages mention how to prepare pollock, including any recommended techniques or seasonings. If no such information is present, I will confirm that the passages do not contain sufficient details to answer the question.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 144.808, "generation_time_seconds": 113.5903, "selection_time_seconds": 31.2109, "nemotron": {"method": "gd", "step_beam_size": 2, "num_rollout": 4, "num_foresight": 3, "runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code"}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "43", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to get plastic out of a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n4. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n\nIf the plastic is still difficult to remove, you can try heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun before attempting to scrape it off. However, if the plastic cannot be removed completely, it may be necessary to replace the drum or the entire dryer.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 71.166, "generation_time_seconds": 40.0027, "selection_time_seconds": 31.1615, "nemotron": {"method": "gd", "step_beam_size": 2, "num_rollout": 4, "num_foresight": 3, "runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code"}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.36, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "44", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to remove plastic from a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again.\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n\nIf the plastic does not come off with this method, another option is to use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic until it becomes soft and pliable. Then, attempt to peel it off carefully. However, be aware that this method may not work, and in that case, replacing the drum or the entire dryer may be necessary. It is recommended to call a service technician for this type of repair.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to get plastic out of clothes dryer is:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper.\n3. Apply nail polish remover to dissolve the plastic.\n4. Rinse with a damp cloth and soap solution.\n5. Use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic if necessary.\n\nIf the plastic still does not come off, consider replacing the drum or the entire dryer.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 72.766, "generation_time_seconds": 40.4231, "selection_time_seconds": 32.3411, "nemotron": {"method": "gd", "step_beam_size": 2, "num_rollout": 4, "num_foresight": 3, "runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code"}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 4.19, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
