{"id": "112", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between the Windward Islands and the Leeward Islands is their exposure to the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies). The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind and are therefore wetter and receive more rainfall, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier, but still receive some rainfall. Additionally, the Windward Islands are located southeast of the Caribbean Sea, while the Leeward Islands are located northwest of the Caribbean Sea.", "pred": "The windward islands are on the eastern side of the Lesser Antilles with steep, mountainous slopes and heavy rainfall, while the leeward islands are on the western side with lower, more arid terrain and less rainfall.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: The windward islands are on the eastern side of the Lesser Antilles with steep, mountainous slopes and heavy rainfall, while the leeward islands are on the western side with lower, more arid terrain and less rainfall.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the key geographical features mentioned for each island group:\n   - Windward Islands: described as \"the eastern, windward side of the Lesser Antilles\" with \"steep, mountainous slopes\" and \"heavy rainfall\"\n   - Leeward Islands: described as \"the western, leeward side of the Lesser Antilles\" with \"lower, more arid\" conditions and \"less rainfall\"\n2. Compare the physical characteristics described for each group:  \n   - Windward Islands exhibit \"steep, mountainous slopes\" and receive \"heavy rainfall.\"  \n   - Leeward Islands are characterized by \"lower, more arid\" terrain and \"less rainfall.\"\n3. Analyze the precipitation patterns described for each group:  \n   - Windward Islands are explicitly associated with \"heavy rainfall.\"  \n   - Leeward Islands are explicitly associated with \"less rainfall.\"\n\nAnswer: The windward islands are on the eastern side of the Lesser Antilles with steep, mountainous slopes and heavy rainfall, while the leeward islands are on the western side with lower, more arid terrain and less rainfall.", "time_sec": 243.9, "generation_time_seconds": 210.4182, "selection_time_seconds": 33.4801, "nemotron": {"method": "gd", "step_beam_size": 2, "num_rollout": 4, "num_foresight": 3, "runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code"}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 20.29, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
